body: "## Problem\n\n`importDir` validates each source with `lstat(path)`, and then reads it with a separate `readFile(path)` (`src/transfer.ts`, `sources()`). If another process replaces the file between the two calls:\n\n- a symlink swapped in for a regular file makes the import read a file **outside the selected directory**, although the regular-file check passed;\n- a larger replacement passes the pre-read size check, so the aggregate size bound runs only after the whole file has been allocated;\n- directory traversal has the same gap for an ancestor that is replaced during the walk.\n\nThis is the same on `main`. pm-memory#51 adds the aggregate size checks but not handle-bound reads (review thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc625ee6).\n\n## Expected\n\n- Open each source with no-follow semantics (`O_NOFOLLOW` where the platform has it) and validate the **opened handle** with `fstat`: regular file, size within the remaining aggregate budget.\n- Read through that handle with a bounded read, so the budget is enforced before allocation.\n- Walk directories through opened directory handles, or re-verify each ancestor's device and inode after reading, so that replacing an ancestor refuses the import with no write.\n- Refusals keep today's typed `MemoryError` codes and redacted diagnostics.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A test that swaps a source file for a symlink between validation and read gets a refusal and no outside bytes.\n- A test that grows a file past the budget after validation gets a refusal before more than the budget is read.\n- A test that retargets an ancestor during the walk gets a refusal.\n- Ordinary imports produce byte-identical results to today."
